# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VirusTotal API key  (required for VT scan)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vt-cli uses the official VirusTotal API, so an API key is always required
# for the VirusTotal scan. Without it, the VT scan is automatically skipped.
#
# How to get a free key:
#   1. Register at https://www.virustotal.com/gui/join-us
#   2. After signing in, open https://www.virustotal.com/gui/my-apikey
#   3. Copy your key and paste it below
#
# Free tier limits:
#   - 4 requests per minute
#   - 500 requests per day
#   - File upload limit: 650 MB
VT_API_KEY=

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub personal access token  (optional)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used only for one API call: fetching the latest GitHub Release info
# (https://api.github.com/repos/owner/repo/releases/latest).
#
# Without a token: 60 requests/hour (anonymous GitHub API limit).
#                  Sufficient for occasional one-off scans.
#
# With a token:    5,000 requests/hour. Only needed if you run the scanner
#                  very frequently (e.g. in CI across many repositories)
#                  or want to scan private repositories.
#
# How to generate (no scopes needed for public repos):
#   https://github.com/settings/tokens  →  Generate new token (classic)
#   → leave all checkboxes unchecked → Generate token
GITHUB_TOKEN=
